 "notes": "Boundary of the red 'Excluded by GW170817 data' region in Fig. 3 (BoundsNSMFull.pdf, vector paths extracted with pymupdf; axes calibrated to the frame spanning 1-3000 MeV and 1e-12-1e-7 GeV^-1, log-log). The excluded region is a closed contour, so points trace the full boundary (not monotonic in mass): starting at (1 MeV, 1e-7 GeV^-1), down the left edge, along the lower limit (minimum g_agamma ~5.1e-11 GeV^-1 near 150-240 MeV, matching the abstract's 'down to 5e-11'), to the right tip at ~362 MeV, back along the upper boundary, and along the top plot edge at g=1e-7 GeV^-1 (the region is clipped there for m < ~55 MeV; larger couplings are covered by SN cooling/low-energy SNe bounds). The shaded region corresponds to the thick solid contour, the 1.25-1.45 Msun asymmetric merger with SFHo EoS; DD2 and symmetric-merger variants are shown only as thin/dashed lines. Bound derived from 90% C.L. X-ray fluence upper limits (CALET CGBM, Konus-Wind, Insight-HXMT/HE) on GW170817/GRB 170817A (Table I). Astrophysical decay bound: no dark-matter density assumption.",
